(Bombay High Court) '
(Anand Prafullchand Tandure vs Income Tax Officer Ward 1 And Others on 10 September, 2026) '
(Author: Nitin B. Suryawanshi) '
(Bench: Nitin B. Suryawanshi) '
(CNR No : HCBM030195642025) '
({1} 975-wp-6367-2025) '
(IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE OF BOMBAY) '
(BENCH AT AURANGABAD) '
(975 WRIT PETITION NO. 6367 OF 2025) '
(Anand Prafullchand Tandure) '
(VERSUS) '
(Income Tax Officer Ward 1 Latur And Others) '
(...) '
(Ms. Rutuja N. Pawar a/w Ms. Sneha More and Ms. Pranaya Ramesh,) '
(Advocates for the Petitioner) '
(Mrs. Kalpalata Patil Bharaswadkar, Senior Standing Counsel for) '
(Respondents No. 1 and 2) '
(Mr. R.R. Bangar, Advocate for Respondents No. 3 and 4) '
(.......) '
(CORAM : NITIN B. SURYAWANSHI AND) '
(ABASAHEB D. SHINDE, JJ.) '
(DATE : 10th SEPTEMBER, 2026) '
(PER COURT :) '
(1. This petition challenges the notice issued under Section 148 of) '
(the Income Tax Act, 1961, dated 29.03.2025 for the assessment year) '
(2019-2020 on various grounds.) '
(2. It is the case of the Petitioner that the impugned notice is) '
(beyond the period of three years as contemplated by Section 149\(1\)) '
(\(b\) of the Income Tax Act, said notice is issued on the alleged escaped) '
(income of Rs. 29,49,958/-, which is less than 50 Lakhs and therefore) '
(same is without jurisdiction and time barred. Another ground is that) '
(the alleged escaped income chargeable to tax in the present case does) '
(not pertain to or is not represented in the form of "an asset".) '
(Therefore, the impugned notice is vitiated.) '
(Uploaded on - - Downloaded on - 16/09/2026 21:32:41) '
({2} 975-wp-6367-2025) '
(In support of the submissions reliance is placed on the decision) '
(of Delhi High Court in Mohd. Athar Anjum vs. Assistant Commissioner) '
(of Income-tax, W.P.\(C\) No. 4196 of 2025 and L-1 Identity Solutions) '
(Operating Company \(P.\) Ltd. vs. Assistant Commissioner of Income-) '
(tax, W.P. \(C\) No. 4845 of 2025.) '
(3. Learned Advocate for Respondents No. 1 and 2 opposed the) '
(petition by relying on para 6 of decision in M/s. Godrej Sara Lee) '
(Limited vs. The Excise and Taxation Officer-Cum- Assessing Authority) '
(and Others, \(2023\) AIR \(SC\) 781, thereby questioning the) '
(maintainability of the petition.) '
(4. We are of the view that Petitioner has made out a prima facie) '
(case for grant of ad-interim relief.) '
(5. Issue notice for final disposal to the respondents, returnable on) '
(08.10.2026.) '
(6. Mrs. Kalpalata Patil Bharaswadkar, Senior Standing Counsel) '
(waives service of notice for Respondents No. 1 and 2. Learned) '
(Advocate Mr. R.R. Bangar waives service of notice for Respondents No.) '
(3 and 4.) '
(7. In the meanwhile, there shall be ad-interim relief in terms of) '
ET
